Subject: [PATCH 01909/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A3
 (HEADLINE DISAMBIGUATION; independent) -- the SAME oracle-distinct beats-vote
 test on CODE, where data is BALANCED and power is HIGH. Train a LEARNED
 pass/fail predictor over sampled code candidates from CACHED corpora
 (HumanEval/MBPP/EvalPlus rerank pools) using ONLY oracle-distinct features
 (the candidate code text + cross-candidate agreement -- NO test execution at
 inference; the hidden-test label is the TRAINING TARGET only, so
 verifier_is_oracle=false). Then the beats-vote gate: predictor@1 vs vote@1 vs
 matched control vs oracle@K, task-level bootstrap CI95-excl-0, N as large as
 the cached pool allows (code has ~0.6 pass-rate vs ARC's 0.008 base-rate ->
 far less imbalance + far more positives). PURPOSE: disambiguate whether the
 .391 ARC null was DATA-SPARSITY (code wins) or a real selection-thesis bound
 (code also ties). Honest null is COMPLETE. STOP re-running CIRCULAR
 code-execution selection -- this is the oracle-DISTINCT (no-execution)
 learned predictor.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
